r non-rectangular elements — ",[22,1059,270],{}," follows the alpha shape (PNG icons, SVGs, ",[22,1062,831],{},"-ed elements), while ",[22,1065,366],{}," is always rectangular. For a circular avatar, ",[22,1068,270],{}," gives a circular shadow.",[692,1071,1072,1051,1074,1077,1078,1081,1082,1084],{},[1048,1073,1050],{},[22,1075,1076],{},"backdrop-filter: blur()"," with a translucent background for glassmorphism — ",[22,1079,1080],{},"background: rgba(255,255,255,0.2); backdrop-filter: blur(10px);"," creates frosted glass. Keep the background translucent (to see the blur) and use ",[22,1083,501],{}," sparingly (it's expensive).",[692,1086,1087,1051,1089,1091,1092,1094,1095,1098,1099,1101],{},[1048,1088,1050],{},[22,1090,818],{}," with a ",[22,1093,769],{}," for soft fade-outs — ",[22,1096,1097],{},"mask: linear-gradient(to bottom, black, transparent)"," fades an element to transparent, something ",[22,1100,831],{}," can't do (it hard-clips). Useful for scroll fade effects.",[692,1103,1104,1051,1106,1109,1110,1112],{},[1048,1105,1050],{},[22,1107,1108],{},"mix-blend-mode: difference"," for guaranteed-contrast text — text with ",[22,1111,1108],{}," against white becomes black, against black becomes white, adapting to any backdrop. Useful for overlays on variable backgrounds.",[692,1114,1115,1051,1117,1120,1121,1124,1125,1128],{},[1048,1116,1050],{},[22,1118,1119],{},"filter: hue-rotate()"," for theming without re-exporting assets — a colored icon can be hue-shifted to match a theme. Combine with ",[22,1122,1123],{},"saturate()","\u002F",[22,1126,1127],{},"brightness()"," for fuller control.",[18,1130,1132],{"id":1131},"️-edge-cases-gotchas","⚠️ Edge Cases & Gotchas",[689,1134,1135,1156,1164,1178,1189,1203,1219,1232,1253,1263],{},[692,1136,1137,1142,1143,1145,1146,644,1149,1151,1152,1155],{},[1048,1138,1139,1141],{},[22,1140,20],{}," creates a stacking context",": like ",[22,1144,719],{}," and ",[22,1147,1148],{},"transform",[22,1150,20],{}," traps children's ",[22,1153,1154],{},"z-index",". A filtered parent's children can't escape its stacking context.",[692,1157,1158,1163],{},[1048,1159,1160,1162],{},[22,1161,501],{}," is expensive",": it samples and filters the backdrop each frame. On large areas or animated elements, it can drop frames. Use on small areas, avoid animating.",[692,1165,1166,1171,1172,1175,1176,687],{},[1048,1167,1168,1170],{},[22,1169,501],{}," needs a translucent background",": with an opaque background, there's nothing to see through, so the blur is invisible. Use ",[22,1173,1174],{},"rgba(...,0.x)"," or ",[22,1177,871],{},[692,1179,1180,1185,1186,1188],{},[1048,1181,1182,1184],{},[22,1183,601],{}," blends with the backdrop, not siblings",": it blends with the content ",[373,1187,511],{}," the element (ancestors, earlier siblings), not the element's own children. And it creates a stacking context.",[692,1190,1191,59,1196,1198,1199,1202],{},[1048,1192,1193,1195],{},[22,1194,1108],{}," with mid-gray",[22,1197,671],{}," against ",[22,1200,1201],{},"rgb(128,128,128)"," inverts to the same gray — text disappears on mid-gray backdrops. Use a different mode or background.",[692,1204,1205,1211,1212,1214,1215,1218],{},[1048,1206,1207,363,1209],{},[22,1208,822],{},[22,1210,818],{},": older Safari only supports ",[22,1213,822],{}," with a limited syntax (no ",[22,1216,1217],{},"mask-mode",", different defaults). Include both for cross-browser; test in Safari.",[692,1220,1221,1228,1229,1231],{},[1048,1222,1223,1225,1226],{},[22,1224,818],{}," with ",[22,1227,928],{},": white = visible, black = hidden (opposite of alpha in some contexts). Explicit ",[22,1230,1217],{}," avoids confusion.",[692,1233,1234,1242,1243,644,1245,1248,1249,1252],{},[1048,1235,1236,1238,1239],{},[22,1237,270],{}," has no ",[22,1240,1241],{},"spread",": unlike ",[22,1244,366],{},[22,1246,1247],{},"filter: drop-shadow()"," takes only ",[22,1250,1251],{},"offset-x offset-y blur color"," — no spread.",[692,1254,1255,1258,1259,1262],{},[1048,1256,1257],{},"Filters are GPU-accelerated but have limits",": stacking many filters or applying to large elements can still be expensive. ",[22,1260,1261],{},"filter: blur(50px)"," on a full-screen element is costly.",[692,1264,1265,1270,1271,1274,1275,687],{},[1048,1266,1267,1269],{},[22,1268,501],{}," Safari support",": needs ",[22,1272,1273],{},"-webkit-backdrop-filter"," in older Safari. Include both: ",[22,1276,1277],{},"backdrop-filter: blur(10px); -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(10px);",[18,1279,1281],{"id":1280},"spot-the-bug","🧠 Spot the Bug",[14,1283,1284],{},"A developer creates a glassmorphism card, but the blur isn't showing — the card is just translucent white:",[30,1286,1287],{"language":32},[34,1288,1290],{"className":36,"code":1289,"language":32,"meta":38,"style":38},".glass {\n    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8);   \u002F* mostly opaque *\u002F\n    backdrop-filter: blur(10px);\n}\n",[22,1291,1292,1298,1329,1345],{"__ignoreMap":38},[42,1293,1294,1296],{"class":44,"line":45},[42,1295,524],{"class":48},[42,1297,527],{"class":52},[42,1299,1300,1302,1304,1306,1308,1310,1312,1314,1316,1318,1320,1323,1326],{"class":44,"line":78},[42,1301,532],{"class":56},[42,1303,59],{"class":52},[42,1305,537],{"class":56},[42,1307,65],{"class":52},[42,1309,542],{"class":56},[42,1311,644],{"class":52},[42,1313,542],{"class":56},[42,1315,644],{"class":52},[42,1317,542],{"class":56},[42,1319,644],{"class":52},[42,1321,1322],{"class":56},"0.8",[42,1324,1325],{"class":52},");   ",[42,1327,1328],{"class":100},"\u002F* mostly opaque *\u002F\n",[42,1330,1331,1333,1335,1337,1339,1341,1343],{"class":44,"line":104},[42,1332,563],{"class":56},[42,1334,59],{"class":52},[42,1336,62],{"class":56},[42,1338,65],{"class":52},[42,1340,572],{"class":56},[42,1342,72],{"class":71},[42,1344,558],{"class":52},[42,1346,1347],{"class":44,"line":125},[42,1348,581],{"class":52},[14,1350,1351],{},"What's wrong?",[1353,1354,1355,1359,1366,1369,1449,1455],"details",{},[1356,1357,1358],"summary",{},"Answer",[14,1360,1361,1362,1365],{},"The background is ",[22,1363,1364],{},"rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8)"," — 80% opaque. Only 20% of the backdrop shows through, so the blur is barely visible. The card looks like a solid white panel, not frosted glass.",[14,1367,1368],{},"The fix — use a more translucent background so the blurred backdrop is visible:",[34,1370,1372],{"className":36,"code":1371,"language":32,"meta":38,"style":38},".glass {\n    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);   \u002F* 20% opaque, 80% backdrop shows *\u002F\n    backdrop-filter: blur(10px);\n    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(10px);   \u002F* Safari *\u002F\n}\n",[22,1373,1374,1380,1409,1425,1445],{"__ignoreMap":38},[42,1375,1376,1378],{"class":44,"line":45},[42,1377,524],{"class":48},[42,1379,527],{"class":52},[42,1381,1382,1384,1386,1388,1390,1392,1394,1396,1398,1400,1402,1404,1406],{"class":44,"line":78},[42,1383,532],{"class":56},[42,1385,59],{"class":52},[42,1387,537],{"class":56},[42,1389,65],{"class":52},[42,1391,542],{"class":56},[42,1393,644],{"class":52},[42,1395,542],{"class":56},[42,1397,644],{"class":52},[42,1399,542],{"class":56},[42,1401,644],{"class":52},[42,1403,555],{"class":56},[42,1405,1325],{"class":52},[42,1407,1408],{"class":100},"\u002F* 20% opaque, 80% backdrop shows *\u002F\n",[42,1410,1411,1413,1415,1417,1419,1421,1423],{"class":44,"line":104},[42,1412,563],{"class":56},[42,1414,59],{"class":52},[42,1416,62],{"class":56},[42,1418,65],{"class":52},[42,1420,572],{"class":56},[42,1422,72],{"class":71},[42,1424,558],{"class":52},[42,1426,1427,1430,1432,1434,1436,1438,1440,1442],{"class":44,"line":125},[42,1428,1429],{"class":56},"    -webkit-backdrop-filter",[42,1431,59],{"class":52},[42,1433,62],{"class":56},[42,1435,65],{"class":52},[42,1437,572],{"class":56},[42,1439,72],{"class":71},[42,1441,1325],{"class":52},[42,1443,1444],{"class":100},"\u002F* Safari *\u002F\n",[42,1446,1447],{"class":44,"line":150},[42,1448,581],{"class":52},[14,1450,1451,1452,1454],{},"::\nAlso, ensure there's content ",[373,1453,511],{}," the card to blur — if the card is over a solid background, the blur has nothing to show. Glassmorphism needs a colorful or textured backdrop to be visible.",[14,1456,1457,59,1460,1462,1463,1466],{},[1048,1458,1459],{},"The lesson",[22,1461,501],{}," blurs what shows ",[373,1464,1465],{},"through"," the background. A mostly-opaque background (0.8) hides the blur. Use a translucent background (0.1–0.3) so the blurred backdrop is visible, and ensure there's content behind to blur.",[18,1468,1469],{"id":1356},"Summary",[14,1471,1472,1473,1475,1476,1478,1479,1481,1482,1124,1484,1486,1487,1489,1490,1492],{},"You can now use ",[22,1474,20],{}," (blur\u002Fbrightness\u002Fcontrast\u002Fgrayscale\u002Fetc., ",[22,1477,270],{}," for non-rectangular shadows), ",[22,1480,501],{}," for glassmorphism (with a translucent background), ",[22,1483,601],{},[22,1485,723],{}," for compositing, and ",[22,1488,818],{}," for soft alpha-based cutting (vs ",[22,1491,831],{},"'s hard clip) — while avoiding the stacking-context and translucency traps. Next: CSS variables and theming.",[1494,1495,1496],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sIsaT, html code.shiki .sIsaT{--shiki-default:#6F42C1;--shiki-github-dark:#B392F0}html pre.shiki code .ssxIu, html code.shiki .ssxIu{--shiki-default:#24292E;--shiki-github-dark:#E1E4E8}html pre.shiki code .snvgF, html code.shiki .snvgF{--shiki-default:#005CC5;--shiki-github-dark:#79B8FF}html pre.shiki code .svdQ7, html code.shiki .svdQ7{--shiki-default:#D73A49;--shiki-github-dark:#F97583}html pre.shiki code .sdCPZ, html code.shiki .sdCPZ{--shiki-default:#6A737D;--shiki-github-dark:#6A737D}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-defaul